    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] The title track, \"I Will Survive\", was a cover of the chart topper for Gloria Gaynor in 1978.\n[2] Based on the 1973 French play of the same name by Jean Poiret, it focuses on a gay couple: Georges, the manager of a Saint-Tropez nightclub featuring drag entertainment, and Albin, his romantic partner and star attraction, and the farcical adventures that ensue when Georges's son, Jean-Michel, brings home his fiancée's ultra-conservative parents to meet them.\n[3] The title of the show is derived from the title of a song in the production, \"I Will Survive\", originally sung by Gloria Gaynor.\n[4] The most notable song on the album was Gloria Gaynor's cover of \"I Am What I Am\" from the musical \"La Cage Aux Folles\"."
